IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `types`
IMPORT `chapter-4-exceptions`

§ `Chapters 21 and 22 -- Defamation, criminal intimidation, insult and public mischief`

-- Penal Code 1871 ss 499, 503, 504, 505.
-- The ten exceptions to s 499 are not encoded as tests; the caller asserts
-- `a section 499 exception applies`. See NOTES.md.
-- Source: registers/source-bundle/PC1871.txt.

§§ `Section 499 -- Defamation`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 499"
@export Decide whether the speech constitutes defamation under Penal Code 1871 section 499
GIVEN s IS A Speech @desc Making or publishing an imputation concerning any person, by words spoken or intended to be read or by signs or visible representations, intending to harm or knowing or having reason to believe it will harm that person reputation. Explanation 4: no harm unless the imputation lowers character, calling or credit in the estimation of others. Set a section 499 exception applies if First to Tenth Exception is met (truth for the public good, good-faith comment on public servants or public questions, substantially true court or Parliament reports, and the remaining exceptions).
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes defamation` IF
        s's `makes or publishes an imputation concerning any person`
    AND s's `by words spoken or intended to be read or by signs or visible representations`
    AND s's `intends to harm or knows or has reason to believe the imputation will harm that person reputation`
    AND s's `the imputation would lower that person character credit or calling in the estimation of others`
    AND NOT s's `a section 499 exception applies`

§§ `Section 503 -- Criminal intimidation`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 503"
@export Decide whether the speech constitutes criminal intimidation under Penal Code 1871 section 503
GIVEN s IS A Speech @desc A threat of injury to person, reputation or property (or of a person in whom the threatened person is interested) with intent to cause alarm, or to cause the person to do something they are not legally bound to do, or to omit something they are legally entitled to do, as the means of avoiding the threat.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes criminal intimidation` IF
        (   s's `threatens another with injury to person reputation or property`
         OR s's `or to the person or reputation of anyone in whom that person is interested`)
    AND (   s's `intent to cause alarm`
         OR s's `intent to cause that person to do an act the person is not legally bound to do`
         OR s's `intent to cause that person to omit an act the person is legally entitled to do`)

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 506"
GIVEN s IS A Speech
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the criminal intimidation attracts the s 506 aggravated punishment` IF
        `constitutes criminal intimidation` s
    AND s's `the threat is to cause death or grievous hurt or destruction of property by fire`

§§ `Section 504 -- Intentional insult with intent to provoke a breach of the peace`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 504"
@export Decide whether the speech is an intentional insult with intent to provoke a breach of the peace under Penal Code 1871 section 504
GIVEN s IS A Speech @desc Intentional insult giving provocation, intending or knowing it likely that the provocation will cause a breach of the public peace or any other offence.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes intentional insult to provoke a breach of the peace` IF
        s's `intentionally insults and thereby gives provocation`
    AND s's `intending or knowing it likely the provocation will cause a breach of the public peace or any other offence`

§§ `Section 505 -- Statements conducing to public mischief`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 505"
@export Decide whether the statement conduces to public mischief under Penal Code 1871 section 505
GIVEN s IS A Speech @desc Making, publishing or circulating a statement, rumour or report in written, electronic or other media with the s 505(b) or (c) intents or likelihoods. The Exception applies where the person has reasonable grounds for believing the statement is true and acts without those intents.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes statements conducing to public mischief` IF
        s's `makes publishes or circulates a statement rumour or report`
    AND s's `in written electronic or other media`
    AND (   s's `intent or likely to cause fear or alarm to the public whereby a person may be induced to commit an offence against the State or public tranquillity`
         OR s's `intent or likely to incite any class or community to commit an offence against any other class or community`)
    AND NOT s's `has reasonable grounds for believing the statement is true and without the intents above`

§§ `Proposed Act wrappers`

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes defamation` IF
        `constitutes defamation` (a's `speech`)
    AND NOT (`a general exception applies` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes criminal intimidation` IF
        `constitutes criminal intimidation` (a's `speech`)
    AND NOT (`a general exception applies` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes intentional insult to provoke a breach of the peace` IF
        `constitutes intentional insult to provoke a breach of the peace` (a's `speech`)
    AND NOT (`a general exception applies` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes statements conducing to public mischief` IF
        `constitutes statements conducing to public mischief` (a's `speech`)
    AND NOT (`a general exception applies` a)

§§ `Illustrations`

`alarming threat` MEANS Speech WITH
    `makes or publishes an imputation concerning any person` IS FALSE
    `by words spoken or intended to be read or by signs or visible representations` IS FALSE
    `intends to harm or knows or has reason to believe the imputation will harm that person reputation` IS FALSE
    `the imputation would lower that person character credit or calling in the estimation of others` IS FALSE
    `a section 499 exception applies` IS FALSE
    `threatens another with injury to person reputation or property` IS TRUE
    `or to the person or reputation of anyone in whom that person is interested` IS FALSE
    `intent to cause alarm` IS TRUE
    `intent to cause that person to do an act the person is not legally bound to do` IS FALSE
    `intent to cause that person to omit an act the person is legally entitled to do` IS FALSE
    `the threat is to cause death or grievous hurt or destruction of property by fire` IS FALSE
    `intentionally insults and thereby gives provocation` IS FALSE
    `intending or knowing it likely the provocation will cause a breach of the public peace or any other offence` IS FALSE
    `makes publishes or circulates a statement rumour or report` IS FALSE
    `in written electronic or other media` IS FALSE
    `intent or likely to cause fear or alarm to the public whereby a person may be induced to commit an offence against the State or public tranquillity` IS FALSE
    `intent or likely to incite any class or community to commit an offence against any other class or community` IS FALSE
    `has reasonable grounds for believing the statement is true and without the intents above` IS FALSE

`true public-good imputation` MEANS Speech WITH
    `makes or publishes an imputation concerning any person` IS TRUE
    `by words spoken or intended to be read or by signs or visible representations` IS TRUE
    `intends to harm or knows or has reason to believe the imputation will harm that person reputation` IS TRUE
    `the imputation would lower that person character credit or calling in the estimation of others` IS TRUE
    `a section 499 exception applies` IS TRUE
    `threatens another with injury to person reputation or property` IS FALSE
    `or to the person or reputation of anyone in whom that person is interested` IS FALSE
    `intent to cause alarm` IS FALSE
    `intent to cause that person to do an act the person is not legally bound to do` IS FALSE
    `intent to cause that person to omit an act the person is legally entitled to do` IS FALSE
    `the threat is to cause death or grievous hurt or destruction of property by fire` IS FALSE
    `intentionally insults and thereby gives provocation` IS FALSE
    `intending or knowing it likely the provocation will cause a breach of the public peace or any other offence` IS FALSE
    `makes publishes or circulates a statement rumour or report` IS FALSE
    `in written electronic or other media` IS FALSE
    `intent or likely to cause fear or alarm to the public whereby a person may be induced to commit an offence against the State or public tranquillity` IS FALSE
    `intent or likely to incite any class or community to commit an offence against any other class or community` IS FALSE
    `has reasonable grounds for believing the statement is true and without the intents above` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `constitutes criminal intimidation` `alarming threat`
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes defamation` `true public-good imputation`)

